# No TAK / operational secrets in this repo

WinTAKTracker is public (`CopIXus/WinTAKTracker`). Treat the tree as visible to the world.

## Never add to git, PRs, issues, docs, screenshots, or samples

- Real TAK server hostnames, FQDNs, or IPs
- Ports tied to real infrastructure when combined with a real host
- Usernames, passwords, API tokens, enrollment tokens
- Callsigns or team names that identify real users/units
- Client certificates, CA/trust stores (`.p12`, `.pfx`, `.pem`, `.key`, SoftCert ZIPs)
- Live Portal / OpenTAK Tracker enroll URLs (`opentaktracker://…`, `tak://…` with real query params)
- Private CloudTAK URLs or SSO cookies/session material
- GPS dumps, debug logs, or config exports containing the above

## Where private data lives

- Runtime only: `%LocalAppData%\WinTAKTracker\` (config, DPAPI secrets, certs, logs, updates)
- Developer scratch: `local/`, `*.local.json`, `.env*` (gitignored)

## Examples in the repo

- Use obvious fakes only: `tak.example.com`, `USER`, `TOKEN`, `CALLSIGN`
- Prefer `samples/enrollment.example.txt` and `samples/config.example.json`
- Redact hosts/tokens in bug reports; never paste live enroll URLs into the repo

## Rule of thumb

If it would let someone join a real TAK network, it does not belong here.
